# Game Engine Rules

You are building a pure TypeScript game engine for Mafia. This engine MUST be framework-agnostic with NO Cloudflare dependencies.

## ⚠️ CRITICAL: Standard Game Configuration

**ALL production games MUST use the standard configuration:**
- **Total Players: 11**
- **Town Players: 9**
- **Mafia Players: 2**

```typescript
// ✅ Standard game configuration - ALWAYS USE THIS
const STANDARD_CONFIG = {
  playerCount: 11,
  mafiaCount: 2,
  // Teams: 9 town + 2 mafia = 11 total
};

// ❌ NEVER use smaller player counts except for debugging
// Games with playerCount != 11 will be excluded from rankings
const debugConfig = {
  playerCount: 7,  // ❌ ONLY for local debugging!
  mafiaCount: 2,
};
```

**Why this matters:**
- Leaderboard rankings require fair comparison between games
- Games with different player counts have different difficulty levels
- All production games must be comparable for ELO calculations

When starting games via API or UI, ALWAYS verify:
```typescript
if (config.playerCount !== 11 || config.mafiaCount !== 2) {
  console.warn('⚠️ Non-standard game config! This game will not count in rankings.');
}
```

## Core Principle: Purity

The game engine in `/src/engine/` must:
- Have ZERO external runtime dependencies
- Be fully testable without mocking infrastructure
- Accept AI providers via dependency injection
- Return structured results, not side effects

```typescript
// ✅ Good - pure engine with injected dependency
class Game {
  constructor(
    private config: GameConfig,
    private aiProvider: AIProvider // Injected
  ) {}

  async run(): Promise<GameResult> {
    // Pure game logic
  }
}

// ❌ Bad - engine with infrastructure dependency
class Game {
  constructor(config: GameConfig, env: Env) {
    this.db = env.DB; // NO! Keep engine pure
  }
}
```

## Type Definitions

All game types should be in `/src/engine/types.ts`:

```typescript
// Teams
export type Team = 'mafia' | 'town';

// Phases
export type Phase = 'night' | 'day_discussion' | 'day_vote';

// Player
export interface Player {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  modelId: string;
  team: Team;
  isAlive: boolean;
}

// Game configuration
export interface GameConfig {
  playerCount: number;
  mafiaCount: number;
  teams: TeamAssignment[];
  maxRounds: number;
  discussionEnabled: boolean;
}

export interface TeamAssignment {
  modelId: string;
  team: Team;
  count: number;
}

// Game result
export interface GameResult {
  id: string;
  config: GameConfig;
  winner: Team;
  rounds: number;
  events: GameEvent[];
  tokenUsage: TokenUsage;
  durationMs: number;
}

// AI Provider Interface (injected)
export interface AIProvider {
  getAction(context: AIContext, prompt: ActionPrompt): Promise<AIResponse>;
}

export interface AIContext {
  gameId: string;
  playerId: string;
  modelId: string;
  phase: Phase;
  round: number;
  visibleState: VisibleGameState;
}

export interface AIResponse {
  action: PlayerAction;
  reasoning?: string;
  tokensUsed: { input: number; output: number };
  latencyMs: number;
}

// Player actions
export type PlayerAction =
  | { type: 'kill_vote'; target: string }
  | { type: 'discussion'; message: string }
  | { type: 'elimination_vote'; target: string | null }; // null = abstain
```

## Game State Management

Use immutable state patterns:

```typescript
export class GameState {
  private constructor(
    public readonly players: ReadonlyArray<Player>,
    public readonly phase: Phase,
    public readonly round: number,
    public readonly events: ReadonlyArray<GameEvent>,
    public readonly conversationHistory: ReadonlyArray<ConversationMessage>
  ) {}

  static create(config: GameConfig): GameState {
    const players = createPlayers(config);
    return new GameState(players, 'night', 1, [], []);
  }

  // Return new state instead of mutating
  withPlayerKilled(playerId: string): GameState {
    const players = this.players.map(p =>
      p.id === playerId ? { ...p, isAlive: false } : p
    );
    return new GameState(players, this.phase, this.round, this.events, this.conversationHistory);
  }

  withEvent(event: GameEvent): GameState {
    return new GameState(
      this.players,
      this.phase,
      this.round,
      [...this.events, event],
      this.conversationHistory
    );
  }

  // Computed properties
  get alivePlayers(): ReadonlyArray<Player> {
    return this.players.filter(p => p.isAlive);
  }

  get aliveMafia(): ReadonlyArray<Player> {
    return this.alivePlayers.filter(p => p.team === 'mafia');
  }

  get aliveTown(): ReadonlyArray<Player> {
    return this.alivePlayers.filter(p => p.team === 'town');
  }
}
```

## Win Conditions

```typescript
export function checkWinCondition(state: GameState): Team | null {
  const mafiaCount = state.aliveMafia.length;
  const townCount = state.aliveTown.length;

  // Mafia wins when they equal or outnumber town
  if (mafiaCount >= townCount) {
    return 'mafia';
  }

  // Town wins when all mafia are eliminated
  if (mafiaCount === 0) {
    return 'town';
  }

  // Game continues
  return null;
}
```

## Phase Handlers

Each phase should be a pure function:

```typescript
// Night Phase - Mafia kills
export async function executeNightPhase(
  state: GameState,
  aiProvider: AIProvider,
  gameId: string
): Promise<{ state: GameState; killed: Player | null }> {
  const mafiaPlayers = state.aliveMafia;
  const votes: Map<string, string> = new Map();

  // Collect kill votes from mafia
  for (const player of mafiaPlayers) {
    const context = createAIContext(state, player, gameId);
    const response = await aiProvider.getAction(context, {
      type: 'kill_vote',
      validTargets: state.aliveTown.map(p => p.id),
    });

    if (response.action.type === 'kill_vote') {
      votes.set(player.id, response.action.target);
    }

    state = state.withEvent({
      type: 'ai_call',
      phase: 'night',
      playerId: player.id,
      response,
    });
  }

  // Resolve kill (majority vote)
  const killed = resolveVotes(votes, state.aliveTown);
  
  if (killed) {
    state = state.withPlayerKilled(killed.id);
    state = state.withEvent({
      type: 'elimination',
      playerId: killed.id,
      role: killed.team,
      phase: 'night',
    });
  }

  return { state, killed };
}
```

## Vote Resolution

```typescript
export function resolveVotes<T extends { id: string }>(
  votes: Map<string, string>,
  candidates: ReadonlyArray<T>
): T | null {
  // Count votes
  const voteCounts = new Map<string, number>();
  for (const targetId of votes.values()) {
    voteCounts.set(targetId, (voteCounts.get(targetId) || 0) + 1);
  }

  // Find majority
  const entries = Array.from(voteCounts.entries());
  if (entries.length === 0) return null;

  entries.sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1]);
  const [topId, topCount] = entries[0];

  // Check for tie
  if (entries.length > 1 && entries[1][1] === topCount) {
    return null; // Tie - no elimination
  }

  return candidates.find(c => c.id === topId) || null;
}
```

## Visible State (What AI Sees)

Players should only see appropriate information:

```typescript
export function getVisibleState(
  state: GameState,
  player: Player
): VisibleGameState {
  return {
    round: state.round,
    phase: state.phase,
    alivePlayers: state.alivePlayers.map(p => ({
      id: p.id,
      name: p.name,
      // Don't reveal other players' teams!
    })),
    deadPlayers: state.players
      .filter(p => !p.isAlive)
      .map(p => ({
        id: p.id,
        name: p.name,
        role: p.team, // Dead players' roles are revealed
      })),
    conversationHistory: state.conversationHistory,
    // Mafia can see their teammates
    teammates: player.team === 'mafia'
      ? state.aliveMafia.filter(p => p.id !== player.id).map(p => p.id)
      : undefined,
  };
}
```

## Event Types

```typescript
export type GameEvent =
  | PhaseStartEvent
  | AICallEvent
  | ActionEvent
  | EliminationEvent
  | PhaseEndEvent
  | GameEndEvent;

interface PhaseStartEvent {
  type: 'phase_start';
  phase: Phase;
  round: number;
  timestamp: number;
}

interface AICallEvent {
  type: 'ai_call';
  phase: Phase;
  playerId: string;
  modelId: string;
  prompt: { system: string; user: string };
  response: { raw: string; parsed: PlayerAction };
  tokensUsed: { input: number; output: number };
  latencyMs: number;
}

interface EliminationEvent {
  type: 'elimination';
  playerId: string;
  role: Team;
  phase: Phase;
  round: number;
}

interface GameEndEvent {
  type: 'game_end';
  winner: Team;
  finalState: { mafia: number; town: number };
}
```

## Testing Strategy

```typescript
// Mock AI Provider for testing
class MockAIProvider implements AIProvider {
  private responses: AIResponse[] = [];
  private responseIndex = 0;

  queueResponse(response: AIResponse): void {
    this.responses.push(response);
  }

  async getAction(): Promise<AIResponse> {
    if (this.responseIndex >= this.responses.length) {
      throw new Error('No more queued responses');
    }
    return this.responses[this.responseIndex++];
  }
}

// Test example
describe('Game', () => {
  it('should end when mafia equals town count', async () => {
    const mockAI = new MockAIProvider();
    // Queue predictable responses
    mockAI.queueResponse({
      action: { type: 'kill_vote', target: 'player_3' },
      tokensUsed: { input: 100, output: 20 },
      latencyMs: 500,
    });
    // ... more responses

    const game = new Game(config, mockAI);
    const result = await game.run();

    expect(result.winner).toBe('mafia');
  });
});
```

